Drop the PROD trust anchor here as ca.cert.pem (needed so a freshly flashed board
trusts future OTA updates):

  scripts/gen-prod-keys.sh                 # once; keys stay in ~/.shareframe-release-keys
  cp ~/.shareframe-release-keys/ca.cert.pem configs/per-device/<name>/overlay/etc/rauc/ca.cert.pem

This overlay applies after packages, so it replaces the dev CA from
package/shareframe-rauc/files/. The CA cert is public — committing it is fine; the
private keys must never enter the repo.

A per-device config is for the ONE-TIME SD flash (it also carries this device's
secret seeds under overlay/usr/share/shareframe/*.default). Build OTA updates from
a configs/fleet/<env>/ config instead — never from here.
